{
  "family": "horn",
  "archetypes": [
    {
      "key": "pyramidal_horn",
      "name": "Pyramidal horn (optimum gain)",
      "family": "horn",
      "summary": "Rectangular waveguide flared in both planes, proportioned for maximum gain at a given length.",
      "freq_range_hz": [
        300000000.0,
        300000000000.0
      ],
      "parameters": [
        {
          "symbol": "f0",
          "name": "design frequency",
          "unit": "Hz",
          "role": "requirement"
        },
        {
          "symbol": "G_target",
          "name": "target gain",
          "unit": "dBi",
          "role": "requirement",
          "typical": "20"
        },
        {
          "symbol": "G0",
          "name": "target gain, linear",
          "unit": "-",
          "role": "derived"
        },
        {
          "symbol": "a1",
          "name": "aperture width (H-plane)",
          "unit": "m",
          "role": "geometry"
        },
        {
          "symbol": "b1",
          "name": "aperture height (E-plane)",
          "unit": "m",
          "role": "geometry"
        },
        {
          "symbol": "rho",
          "name": "flare length",
          "unit": "m",
          "role": "geometry"
        },
        {
          "symbol": "lambda0",
          "name": "free-space wavelength",
          "unit": "m",
          "role": "derived"
        }
      ],
      "synthesis": [
        {
          "output": "G0",
          "expr": "undb10(G_target)",
          "units_out": "-",
          "depends_on": [
            "G_target"
          ]
        },
        {
          "output": "rho",
          "expr": "G0*(c/f0)/(0.51*4*pi*np.sqrt(6))",
          "units_out": "m",
          "depends_on": [
            "G0",
            "f0"
          ],
          "notes": "Equal-slant approximation rho_e = rho_h = rho. Substituting the optimum-gain conditions into G = 0.51*4*pi*a1*b1/lambda^2 gives G0 = 15.6984*rho/lambda exactly."
        },
        {
          "output": "a1",
          "expr": "np.sqrt(3*(c/f0)*rho)",
          "units_out": "m",
          "depends_on": [
            "f0",
            "rho"
          ],
          "notes": "optimum-gain H-plane condition a1 = sqrt(3*lambda*rho_h)"
        },
        {
          "output": "b1",
          "expr": "np.sqrt(2*(c/f0)*rho)",
          "units_out": "m",
          "depends_on": [
            "f0",
            "rho"
          ],
          "notes": "optimum-gain E-plane condition b1 = sqrt(2*lambda*rho_e)"
        }
      ],
      "analysis": [
        {
          "metric": "aperture_area_m2",
          "expr": "a1*b1",
          "units_out": "m^2",
          "depends_on": [
            "a1",
            "b1"
          ]
        },
        {
          "metric": "gain_dbi",
          "expr": "db10(0.51*4*pi*a1*b1*(f0/c)**2)",
          "units_out": "dBi",
          "depends_on": [
            "a1",
            "b1",
            "f0"
          ],
          "notes": "Forward check against the synthesised aperture; must return G_target. 0.51 is the standard optimum-pyramidal aperture efficiency, which already embeds the quadratic phase-error loss over the flared aperture."
        },
        {
          "metric": "aperture_efficiency",
          "expr": "0.51",
          "units_out": "-"
        },
        {
          "metric": "hpbw_e_deg",
          "expr": "54.1/(b1*f0/c)",
          "units_out": "deg",
          "depends_on": [
            "b1",
            "f0"
          ],
          "notes": "E-plane HPBW = 54.1*lambda/b1 for an optimum horn"
        },
        {
          "metric": "hpbw_h_deg",
          "expr": "78.1/(a1*f0/c)",
          "units_out": "deg",
          "depends_on": [
            "a1",
            "f0"
          ],
          "notes": "H-plane HPBW = 78.1*lambda/a1 for an optimum horn"
        },
        {
          "metric": "directivity_from_beamwidths_dbi",
          "expr": "db10(26000/((54.1/(b1*f0/c))*(78.1/(a1*f0/c))))",
          "units_out": "dBi",
          "depends_on": [
            "a1",
            "b1",
            "f0"
          ],
          "notes": "Independent cross-check via D ~ 26000/(theta_E*theta_H). Agrees with the aperture formula to about 0.18 dB, which is the honest accuracy of both."
        },
        {
          "metric": "phase_error_e_plane",
          "expr": "b1**2/(8*(c/f0)*rho)",
          "units_out": "-",
          "depends_on": [
            "b1",
            "f0",
            "rho"
          ],
          "notes": "s = b1^2/(8*lambda*rho_e); the optimum design fixes this at 0.25"
        },
        {
          "metric": "phase_error_h_plane",
          "expr": "a1**2/(8*(c/f0)*rho)",
          "units_out": "-",
          "depends_on": [
            "a1",
            "f0",
            "rho"
          ],
          "notes": "t = a1^2/(8*lambda*rho_h); the optimum design fixes this at 0.375"
        },
        {
          "metric": "axial_length_m",
          "expr": "rho",
          "units_out": "m",
          "depends_on": [
            "rho"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "validity": [
        "optimum-gain proportions only; a horn of arbitrary a1/b1/rho needs the full Fresnel-integral gain expression (Balanis 13-19), not this closed form",
        "the equal-slant simplification rho_e = rho_h is exact for the standard design but a physically realisable pyramidal horn also requires the two flare sections to meet at the waveguide, which constrains rho_e and rho_h separately",
        "G_target above about 30 dBi gives a horn long enough that a reflector is usually the better answer",
        "does not model the waveguide-to-horn junction mismatch"
      ],
      "known_cases": [
        {
          "given": {
            "f0": 10000000000.0,
            "G_target": 20.0
          },
          "expect": {
            "gain_dbi": 20.0,
            "phase_error_e_plane": 0.25,
            "phase_error_h_plane": 0.375
          },
          "tol_pct": 1.0,
          "source": "Self-consistency across independent routes: the optimum-gain dimensions must reproduce the requested gain through G = 0.51*4*pi*a1*b1/lambda^2, and must land on the canonical phase errors s = 1/4 and t = 3/8. Balanis, Antenna Theory 4th ed., Ch. 13"
        },
        {
          "given": {
            "f0": 10000000000.0,
            "G_target": 20.0
          },
          "expect": {
            "a1_m": 0.131094,
            "b1_m": 0.107031,
            "hpbw_e_deg": 15.156,
            "hpbw_h_deg": 17.866
          },
          "tol_pct": 1.0,
          "source": "20 dBi at 10 GHz: a1 = 4.3715 lambda, b1 = 3.5693 lambda; HPBW 15.16 deg (E) and 17.87 deg (H). Balanis, Antenna Theory 4th ed., Ch. 13"
        },
        {
          "given": {
            "f0": 10000000000.0,
            "G_target": 20.0
          },
          "expect": {
            "directivity_from_beamwidths_dbi": 20.0
          },
          "tol_abs": 0.25,
          "source": "Cross-check: D ~ 26000/(theta_E*theta_H) must agree with the aperture-area gain to within the ~0.2 dB accuracy of the beamwidth approximation. Milligan, Modern Antenna Design 2nd ed., Ch. 7"
        }
      ],
      "references": [
        "Balanis, Antenna Theory 4th ed., Ch. 13 (13.4.3, optimum pyramidal horn design)",
        "Milligan, Modern Antenna Design 2nd ed., Ch. 7"
      ]
    },
    {
      "key": "e_plane_sectoral_horn",
      "name": "E-plane sectoral horn (optimum)",
      "family": "horn",
      "summary": "Rectangular waveguide flared in the E-plane only; the H-plane keeps the waveguide's cosine distribution.",
      "freq_range_hz": [
        300000000.0,
        300000000000.0
      ],
      "parameters": [
        {
          "symbol": "f0",
          "name": "design frequency",
          "unit": "Hz",
          "role": "requirement"
        },
        {
          "symbol": "a_wg",
          "name": "unflared waveguide dimension",
          "unit": "m",
          "role": "requirement",
          "typical": "0.02286"
        },
        {
          "symbol": "rho",
          "name": "flare slant length",
          "unit": "m",
          "role": "requirement",
          "typical": "0.3"
        },
        {
          "symbol": "b1",
          "name": "flared aperture dimension",
          "unit": "m",
          "role": "geometry"
        }
      ],
      "synthesis": [
        {
          "output": "b1",
          "expr": "np.sqrt(2*(c/f0)*rho)",
          "units_out": "m",
          "depends_on": [
            "f0",
            "rho"
          ],
          "notes": "optimum condition b1 = sqrt(2*lambda*rho)"
        }
      ],
      "analysis": [
        {
          "metric": "gain_dbi",
          "expr": "db10(0.65*4*pi*b1*a_wg*(f0/c)**2)",
          "units_out": "dBi",
          "depends_on": [
            "b1",
            "a_wg",
            "f0"
          ],
          "notes": "aperture efficiency 0.65 for the optimum E-plane horn"
        },
        {
          "metric": "aperture_efficiency",
          "expr": "0.65",
          "units_out": "-"
        },
        {
          "metric": "aperture_area_m2",
          "expr": "b1*a_wg",
          "units_out": "m^2",
          "depends_on": [
            "b1",
            "a_wg"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "validity": [
        "optimum flare only",
        "the exact gain needs Fresnel integrals (Balanis 13-19/13-41); this closed form is the standard optimum-design shortcut",
        "aperture efficiency figure is the textbook value for the optimum case and does not track departures from it"
      ],
      "known_cases": [
        {
          "given": {
            "f0": 10000000000.0,
            "a_wg": 0.02286,
            "rho": 0.3
          },
          "expect": {
            "b1": 0.13411766281888451
          },
          "tol_pct": 1.5,
          "source": "b1 = sqrt(2*lambda*rho) at 10 GHz with rho = 0.3 m. Balanis, Antenna Theory 4th ed., Ch. 13"
        }
      ],
      "references": [
        "Balanis, Antenna Theory 4th ed., Ch. 13 (13.2, 13.3)"
      ]
    },
